00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.180
Today's dish is a home-cooked meal, "water rice."

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.010
You prepare it by rinsing cold rice with cold water,

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:29.140
and eat it together with side dishes
such as pickles and fish.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.980
Depending on the region,
it is called different names,

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.520
such as "rinsed rice,"
and "rice in cold tea."

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:42.990
Okay!

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.120
What shall we eat with it?

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.160
Just watch!

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:47.790
What?

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:49.830
First, slice a cucumber...

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.620
...and spread it over the water rice.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:57.500
Then, put plum pulp, miso, soy sauce,
and dried bonito on top of it.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.670
Sesame Oil

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.880
And finally, add a drop of sesame oil.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:01.880
Done!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.470
Thanks for the meal!

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.610
Delicious!

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.570
This is amazing!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.070
It's delicious, Machi!

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.610
It's cheap, and healthy.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:23.910
The best CP ratio!

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.950
I know what "CP" is!

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.080
It's short for "cosplay party," right?!

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:32.710
And "cosplay" is short for "costume play,"
where people in costumes gather.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.710
It's a little spicy.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:34.920
I can eat it easily!

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:36.380
Hm?

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.090
I don't remember her using spicy ingredients...

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:42.880
Is this spiciness... possibly...

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.050
Red pepper miso!

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.090
So this is the red pepper miso's spiciness!

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.760
Impressive, Machi.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.390
To think that she used red pepper miso
instead of the regular miso!

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.060
Pretty amazing.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.480
Fuchi makes it every year
out of force of habit,

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.860
but we don't know what to do with it
since we don't eat it that much.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:03.240
And yet, she took the opportunity
and used it in the cold-water rice.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.070
This is amazing!

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.110
You'll be a good wife!

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.160
You're being too flattering!

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:09.530
Too flattering, Natsu!

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:13.500
Okay...

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.710
Then, I'll make it, too.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.500
Natsu is excited by such a small thing.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.460
Put extra ice to the water rice...

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.220
...and scatter arugula.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:28.680
Arugula?

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:33.560
Stir-fry chopped garlic with
olive oil to bring out the aroma.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.230
Olive oil?

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:40.820
There, put bacon and tomato and
stir-fry them until tomato softens.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.070
Add beaten egg.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.650
Once the egg is half-cooked...

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:49.070
...add some basil leaves and fry them quickly.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.950
Put this on top of the water rice.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:57.080
Add salt, pepper and soy sauce to season it.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.380
Lastly add a drop of olive oil.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.340
Now Italian style cold-water rice is ready!

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:10.470
Yep.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.260
I can taste the garlic.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.810
But the affinity between the water rice
and the fried tomato isn't quite...

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:23.480
Whoa!

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.780
Adding some lemon juice made it a lot better!

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:28.530
Hm?

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.530
What's wrong, Machi?

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.330
What's "arugula"?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.160
What's "basil"?!

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.830
What do you mean Italia style?!

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.670
Have you been to Italy?!

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.210
I haven't.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:46.170
Are you saying that city people have to
have detailed knowledge about Italy?!

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:52.470
Well, knowing only pizza buns and spaghetti
with meat sauce could cause you trouble later on...

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:54.720
That's cheeky! That's cheeky!

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:55.060
What?

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.930
You're just Natsu, so don't get cheeky!

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:57.730
Hey, guys!

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:58.350
Geez!

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.060
Oh, having lunch?

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:00.980
That's cheeky!

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:05.320
We were working on some
new recipes for water rice.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:06.730
I see...

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:07.990
Try them and compare!

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.070
Sure.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.620
Oh, this is yummy!

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:17.910
I could eat this all day!

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.290
Whoa!

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.420
Italian style, huh?

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.000
That's stylish!

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.300
Where'd you get basil and arugula?

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.550
They were grown in Tatsuo's field.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:32.590
Really?

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:34.850
I didn't know my old man was growing these.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.810
Which one did you like?

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:37.640
Hm?

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.600
I liked both of them.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:46.570
But, well, as a man,
the more filling meal iiiiiiiiis...

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:48.360
...not necessarily the best one.

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:51.700
Yep, I liked Machi's better.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:53.530
It was like a restaurant food!

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.490
You don't cook every day for nothing!

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:57.790
Really?

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:00.330
Aren't you up to something, Yoshio?

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:00.500
Aren't you up to something, Yoshio-kun?

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.250
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.170
In these health-conscious days,

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:11.220
it's important to eat delicious
and healthy food, isn't it?

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.970
Your food isn't as flashy
as Natsu's, but it's elegant.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.890
Just as you'd expect from a girl.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:21.140
Boys won't leave you alone.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.020
You'll say anything to please people.

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:26.310
And that said...

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:31.190
...what do you think about using
your cooking skills for the village?!

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.610
Now, Natsu, let's clean it up.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.990
I'm not done talking yet.

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:39.240
I knew you were up to something!

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.950
I don't know what it's about, but I decline!

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.410
No, you got it wrong!

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:48.960
I just want you to promote our village's
specialties to many people.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.260
Really, it's a regular part-time job!

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:55.680
You'll just keep cooking food
samples at a supermarket.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:58.180
A part-time job?

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.930
That's right, a part-time job!

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.270
Think of it like a social studies field trip!

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.690
You'll earn some money, too!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:10.520
If things go well, they will
take you to Sendai, too!

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:12.610
Sendai?!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.070
Possibly to Tokyo, too.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.110
Tokyo?!

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.580
I think it'll be a good experience for Machi...

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:26.540
Tokyo?

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.580
T-T-Tokyo?!

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.380
But I think it's a bit too much for her.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.340
And you will wear an outfit
like this for your work.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:37.430
No!

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.050
Please, Machi!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:43.560
I'm begging you!

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:44.930
No! No!

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:46.270
It can't be helped!

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.440
Now that it's come to this...!

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.070
I'll have you write a pledge
even if I have to force you!

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:57.780
Nooooooooo!

00:09:58.360 --> 00:09:59.160
Machi...

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.830
That's amazing! Sendai?!

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.080
I wanna go there, too!

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:09.920
But I can't... so tell me what it's like
when you come back, okay?

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:14.880
Ahh... from now on, you are
more of a city person than I am!

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.920
I-I didn't say that I'd do it-

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.590
Have confidence in yourself, Machi!

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:22.470
Miko outfits like that are trendy
in the city right now!

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.390
You looked good in that outfit, too!

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.480
I like number one, though.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:28.980
Eh?

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:30.860
Trendy?

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:32.310
Yes.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:35.730
There's an unprecedented
miko boom right now.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.870
Mikos are trendy, right, Yoshio?

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:42.410
Huh?

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:45.910
Yeah!

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.540
They're super trendy.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:50.920
You're such a cute miko.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:52.630
If you don't go public, who will?!

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:56.170
You're the one who looks better
in miko outfits than anyone else!

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:00.930
If you say so...

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.010
I guess I can do...

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:06.390
...it.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:33.460
He tricked me.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:35.630
Oh, you shouldn't say such things!

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:38.210
He tricked me... He tricked me...

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:42.970
He tricked me, he tricked me,
he tricked me, he tricked me, he...

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.760
They will take you to Sendai!

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.390
This isn't Sendai.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.560
This is a local supermarket in a nearby area.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:54.980
You'll just keep cooking at a supermarket.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.230
That's what he said.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:59.400
I'll go check other work sites!

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.820
He left me alone.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.610
There was a store specified apron...

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:05.990
...but he had a weird outfit for me!

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.330
I got scolded.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:16.090
And I've been devoting myself
preparing sample food for a while.

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:19.090
I though it would be apples,
but it was actually nameko.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:21.590
And no one's trying them.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:36.650
Mushroom Fair

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:39.610
Do your job, okay?

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:50.040
If you're just standing there,
I'll send you home.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:56.960
This is a staff announcement.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.750
Mr. Tanaka in the produce section,
please pick up line five.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.750
Tanaka-san in the produce section,
please pick up line five.

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.920
Really, do your job, okay?!

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:08.010
I-I wanna go home...

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:13.430
Because... no one ever told me
that it would be this kind of job.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.480
It's his fault.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.770
It's impossible!

00:13:17.770 --> 00:13:20.520
I can't talk to strangers and sell things!

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:25.070
I'm going home.

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.110
It's Yoshio's fault.

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:27.240
It's Yoshio-kun's fault.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.830
I'm going home... I'm going home...

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.120
I'm going home!

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.960
I'm going back... to that mountain!

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.590
Machi!

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.300
Everyone!

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.600
I'm going back... to that river!

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:54.390
But...

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.980
...what will happen to me... if I go home?

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:06.490
If I did, I kinda think that
my life would be over.

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:08.360
I can't run!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:15.660
Nameko...

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.710
Would you like some nameko?!

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:32.760
Voice, echo through this store!

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:36.230
Mom! I want fish meat sausage!

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.560
My son is...

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.180
Nameko...

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.190
...would you like some?

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.560
I want fish meat sausage!

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.190
You had it a lot the other day!

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.190
Nameko...

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:47.030
Yellowtails and tunas are on sale today!

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:47.030
Nameko...

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:53.280
In the meat section, pork ribs are 68 yen
for 100 grams, which is a very good deal.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:57.750
Thank you very much
for shopping again at the Market!

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:00.750
I feel embarrassed.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.290
I feel empty.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:04.130
My heart aches!

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.010
My life is about to disapp-

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.720
What are you doing?

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.050
H-Hibiki?!

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.050
H-Hibiki-chan?!

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:14.260
What are you doing here?

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.430
My work is along the
national highway, too.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:21.060
More importantly, why are you
giving out sample fo-

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:21.600
Hm?

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:25.400
I see...

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.570
Then this is your first time
being a part-timer, huh?

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:29.400
Yeah.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.490
That sounds tough.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:33.370
Well, I don't wanna be in your way, so...

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.280
See ya.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:36.660
Good lu... ck?

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.870
What the hell are you
looking at me like that for?!

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.960
I haven't sold even a single one.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:44.080
And no customer wants
to sample it, either.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.590
So I... I...

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:50.590
Don't cry!

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:53.640
Geez...

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.010
Then I'll be a decoy.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.310
If someone's trying it out...

00:15:57.970 --> 00:15:59.390
...others will probably stop by, too.

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:01.440
Thank you, Hibiki.

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:01.520
Thank you, Hibiki-chan.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.650
I thought I'd die...

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:05.980
Hey, it's gotten cold!

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:08.150
You should make fresh ones!

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:12.950
What the hell is this?!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.280
This is damn good!

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.780
Seriously, this is good!
Give me more!

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:18.540
This nameko is delicious!

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:19.660
This is good nameko!

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:22.790
That girl is being harassed by a delinquent.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.290
Poor girl...

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.380
Well, Tohoku people aren't joiners, you know?

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:32.760
Hey, I'm super desperately trying
to be a decoy for you!

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.970
Why are you being so quiet?!

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.180
Speak up!

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:40.100
Hey, say, "Welcome!"

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.520
W-Welchome.

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:44.230
Look, she's a delinquent.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.650
How scary...

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:47.730
I can't hear you!

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.400
Welcome!

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:50.780
Hey, you can do it!

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:53.490
You should have done it from the start!

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:55.530
Then, I'll get going...

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:58.490
...or I'll run out of time for lunch.

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.620
Thank you, Hibiki.

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.790
Thank you, Hibiki-chan.

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:05.920
I can't hear you.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:15.260
Uhm...

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:29.770
Try harder, Machi.

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:32.480
Tohoku people aren't joiners.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:37.280
I have to try harder!

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.490
Nameko...

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:43.660
Would you like some nameko?!

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.580
Delicious nameko...

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:51.170
How about sampling some?

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.760
Cultivated on withered tree logs.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:55.170
This is delicious...

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:57.340
...nameko...

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.140
Would you lik-

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:05.680
Would you like some?!

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:13.980
How about sampling some?!

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:17.280
How about...

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.450
How about...

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:23.620
...sampling some?!

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.040
Missy...

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.040
Ojou-san...

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.460
May I try some?

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.710
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.720
Th-Thank you very much!

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.340
Missy...

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.470
Ojou-san...

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:42.720
No matter how hard it is,
don't be discouraged, okay?

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:43.970
Yes, ma'am.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:45.810
Hang in there.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:47.480
Don't give in, okay?

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:51.690
Yes, ma'am...

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:59.320
After that, the marketing that was painful
to both Machi and the passersby continued...

00:18:57.990 --> 00:18:59.320
Nameko...

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:03.870
Nameko...! Nameko...!

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:03.280
...but Machi shed no tears.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.870
Hey, hey, hey!

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:08.250
How's it going?!

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:09.960
What's wrong, Machi?

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.830
You look like you're about to die.

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:14.880
I was gone for a bit and now
you look like an old lady.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.010
Y-Yoshio...

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:17.090
Y-Yoshio-kun...

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:21.300
I-I... worked hard...

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:23.970
I did my best...

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:25.970
But it didn't work.

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:29.310
No one will be happy like this.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:29.390
I see...

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.600
It was really tough, huh?

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:34.020
Listen.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:38.320
Basically, Tohoku people don't sample food.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:39.490
I see, I see.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:41.280
It's almost meaningless.

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:42.990
It's very hard...

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:45.240
It's not like this place has no customers...

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:53.290
Welcome to
Kumade Village

00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:50.120
Hi! Welcome! Hello!

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:54.420
We have today's special,
nameko from Kumade Village, here!

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:55.670
It's safe and delicious!

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:59.920
We've got Kumade Village brand nameko here!

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:04.680
We're offering one of our delicious
nameko dishes for sampling!

00:20:04.680 --> 00:20:05.970
What's going on?

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:06.970
Are they doing something?

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.890
Please try it out!

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.730
You don't have to buy it!

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:12.390
What is it?

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:13.600
It's okay to have some?

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:15.270
Sure! Please try it!

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:16.980
Try some!

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:18.070
Oh?

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:19.150
Scrambled eggs with chives, huh?

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:20.190
Let me have one.

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.740
Give me one, too.

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:23.160
May I have one, too?

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:24.910
Sure.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:29.160
We've got the safe and popular
Kumade Village brand nameko here!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.620
The right person for the right job...

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:40.630
Well, it's true that the job
wasn't for you, Machi...

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:42.220
...but I'm impressed!

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:43.930
You bore it and finished the job!

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:48.220
I was worried that you might
ditch the job and come home.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:51.180
It's not true that the job wasn't for me.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:51.980
What?

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:55.100
It was just that Yoshio was
especially good at it, that's all!

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:55.100
It was just that Yoshio-kun was
especially good at it, that's all!

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:57.610
I did sell about five, too.

00:20:58.060 --> 00:21:01.900
But Machi, you can't speak
loudly in front of people.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.990
Even you thought it was beyond you, right?

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:05.200
No, I didn't!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.450
And I spoke up just fine!

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:08.950
What's the matter?

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:11.950
It was really hard.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:15.370
But those who tried it out...

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.920
...said it was delicious.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:21.800
So... I have... decided...

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:25.590
...that I'll promote Kumade's nameko!

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:27.930
You don't have to worry
about nameko anymore.

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:30.680
The part-timer who was
taking the day off will be back.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:36.020
At any rate, I'm glad that you finished
your first job without a hitch!

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:38.270
Thanks for your hard work.

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:42.150
I'm surprised you can do a job where
you have to speak in front of people!

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:46.400
You're up to something else,
aren't you, Yoshio?

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:46.400
You're up to something else,
aren't you, Yoshio-kun?

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:46.990
What?

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:51.080
Maybe not yet,
but I bet he's about to be...

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:53.370
Natsu!

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:28.210
Kumamiko-chan!

00:23:30.380 --> 00:23:32.010
I'm hungry.

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:36.260
I know it's not my place to say this...

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:39.770
...but you're the one who makes dinner...

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:44.940
...so why don't you start on it sooner
and nibble until dinner ti-

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:46.730
Ah. Ah.

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:47.860
I'm sorry!

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:49.150
Ah. Ah. Ah.

00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:54.120
Kumamiko.
